1:1-1 (* EXPECT-ERROR: Column is declared twice in module Table *)
2:1-18 (* This is half a program, silently.  It was observed 2026-10-03:\n   corpus/Csv.m9 had `ColF64' declared twice, since 2026-09-10.  It\n   was the same heading, the same body, a paste nobody saw, and it\n   had shipped in five releases, 0.9.0 to 0.13.0.  Neither checker\n   had a word for a second declaration.  The C compiler would have\n   refused two definitions, but the generator keeps procedures by\n   name.  So it emitted the SECOND body and dropped the first, and\n   the program built and ran.  With identical bodies nothing showed.\n   Had the two differed, the one a reader saw first would be the one\n   that did not run: the one above the fold, the one the\n   documentation page is made from.  The same day a constant in\n   NetCDF was found declared twice, and a second `Ink' in Plot was\n   what led there.\n\n   Here the first Column answers the column, the second answers its\n   first element: a reader sees the first and the program runs the\n   second. *)
34:40-34 (* the first Column has it; the second raises *)
comments=3
